    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "（原書朱印乎黑印カ記セス）"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "（原書、朱印か黒印か記せず）"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Parenthesised editorial note printed as a two-line warichu below the temple-land figure: \"the original manuscript does not record whether [these grants] were vermilion-seal or black-seal.\" Shrine and temple lands were held either as shuinchi (朱印地, granted under the shogun's vermilion seal) or as kokuinchi (黒印地, under a daimyo's black seal); the compilers are flagging that the source they worked from left the category unstated."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "原書朱印乎黑印カ記セス"
      }
    ],
